PARITY (web GuardedLink.tsx → native)
  The web surface is anonymous (no t() of its own): it is a drop-in <Link>/<NavLink> replacement that,
  on a primary click, runs the caller onClick, bails for modifier/middle clicks and target="_blank"
  (shouldSkipGuard), and otherwise awaits confirmIfDirty() before navigate(to,{replace,state,relative}).
  When a registered guard is dirty, confirmIfDirty surfaces the NavigationGuardProvider <ConfirmDialog>.

  Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder seams, no router/HTTP in the view):
    useNavigate                  → GuardedNavigator seam: navigate(to,options) (same context) +
                                   openInNewContext(dest) (the guard-bypass path). The view never
                                   touches the router.
    useNavigationGuardContext    → NavigationGuardSource emits GuardedLinkInput (the controlled `to` +
                                   forwarded replace/relative/state + the live isDirty + the guard's
                                   optional message + the store load/connectivity state). The view never
                                   reads the guard registry.
    useTranslation (provider)    → GuardedLinkStrings P1/S10 facade. The dialog copy is reproduced
                                   VERBATIM under the web forms.* keys (forms.unsavedTitle /
                                   forms.unsavedWarning / forms.discard / forms.keepEditing); native leaf
                                   chrome + the "Open in New Window" affordance are guardedLink.* keys.

  Behaviour (each branch unit-asserted against the web expression):
    shouldSkipGuard              → GuardDecision.shouldSkipGuard: VERBATIM port —
                                   metaKey|ctrlKey|shiftKey|altKey OR button!==0 OR
                                   (target && target!=='' && target!=='_self') ⇒ skip.
    onClick (clean)              → model.activate: confirmIfDirty()==true ⇒ navigator.navigate(to,options).
    onClick (dirty)             → model.activate raises confirmRequest ⇒ the SwiftUI .confirmationDialog
                                   (Discard changes ⇒ confirmDiscard ⇒ navigate; Keep editing ⇒ cancel).
    skip-guard / new tab         → model.activate ⇒ navigator.openInNewContext(dest), guard bypassed so
                                   the current context keeps its unsaved work (Apple-idiomatic
                                   "Open in New Window").
    e.defaultPrevented           → activation.isPreempted ⇒ neither guard nor navigation runs.

STATES (every state renders — no hidden surface)
  loading — guard feed being read → skeleton link chrome.
  empty   — no/blank destination (web `to` empty) → friendly empty state (native improvement; never a
            blank box).
  error   — guard-feed failure with no usable destination → retryable error tile (web QueryError peer).
  data    — the tappable link; primary tap runs the guard-or-navigate flow; context action opens a new
            window/scene; a dirty guard raises the unsaved-changes confirmation.
  stale / offline — orthogonal connectivity axis → freshness chip beneath the link + one-shot
            auto-refresh on the stale transition.

